-- title:
--   Saturated Tate image with free cokernel of toric rank
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the level-$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$. Given a model datum $\mathfrak{X}$ of type [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81), level data $\Lambda$ and an object $O$ of type [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP`](def/ModularCurve_JHNeronObjectAtP.html#L53) over $Pl$, assume that the designations built from $(O.G,O.g)$ and from $(\Lambda.X,\Lambda.f)$, with their identity sections, represent the relative Picard subfunctor cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero on the two-chart integral models of levels $\Gamma_M$ and $\Gamma_N$, rigidified by $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ respectively by $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$. Let $Rh$ be a Henselian local domain, an algebra over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with injective structure map, landing in $Pl$ and with maximal ideal exactly the elements of valuation $<1$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a $p$-divisible group over $Rh$ of height $h$, and $\Delta$ an injective additive map from $\mathcal{G}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field of $X_H$, whose level-$v$ image is exactly $O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^v)$, the subgroup generated by the $p^v$-torsion classes whose associated point extends to a section over $Pl$ along $\Lambda.\sigma_A$. Assume $\#J_H(M)[p^v] = p^{v(h+t)}$ for all $v$, where $t = O.\mathrm{toricRank}$, and let $e$ be an injective $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear map from the Tate module of $\mathcal{G}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to that of $J_H(M)$ (sequences with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p x_{n+1} = x_n$) acting coordinatewise by $\Delta$, whose range consists exactly of the sequences with $y_n \in O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^n)$ for all $n$. Then the range of $e$ is saturated, i.e. $p \cdot y \in \mathrm{range}\, e$ implies $y \in \mathrm{range}\, e$, and there is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear isomorphism from $T_p J_H(M)/\mathrm{range}\, e$ onto $\mathbb{Z}_p^{t}$.
--
--   This is the rank computation in the Tate-module packaging of the finite (connected, $p$-divisible) part of the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$: the finite part sits saturated inside $T_p J_H(M)$ with free quotient of rank the toric rank, matching the $p^{v(h+t)}$ torsion count. It is used in [`ModularCurve.exists_pDivisibleGroup_points_eq_finPts_raynaudExtension_closedImmersion_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_representsRelSubPic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_pDivisibleGroup_points_eq_finPts_raynaudExtension_closedImmersion_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_representsRelSubPic).
